WEBVTT

00:00:06.654 --> 00:00:08.351
Harry!

00:00:08.395 --> 00:00:10.745
[ shouting]

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:16.490
Aresto momentum!

00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:19.493
RON:
He looks a bit peaky,

00:00:19.536 --> 00:00:20.320
doesn't he?

00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:21.364
FRED:
Peaky?

00:00:21.408 --> 00:00:22.539
GEORGE:
What'd you expect?

00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:23.497
FRED:
He fell over 100 feet.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.759
Yeah,
come on, Ron,

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:25.847
let's walk you off
the Astronomy tower...

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.022
And see what you look like.

00:00:27.066 --> 00:00:28.197
HARRY:
Probably a right sight

00:00:28.241 --> 00:00:29.068
better than
he normally does.

00:00:29.111 --> 00:00:32.027
[ chuckling]

00:00:33.724 --> 00:00:34.769
How are you feeling?

00:00:34.812 --> 00:00:35.726
Oh, brilliant.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:36.945
GEORGE:
You gave us

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:38.512
a right good
scare there, mate.

00:00:38.555 --> 00:00:40.035
HARRY:
What happened?

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:41.123
RON:
Well...

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:42.211
you fell off your broom.

00:00:42.255 --> 00:00:43.430
HARRY:Really?

00:00:43.473 --> 00:00:45.954
I meant the match.
Who won?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.306
Um... no one
blames you, Harry.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.701
The dementors aren't supposed
to come inside the grounds.

00:00:53.744 --> 00:00:55.137
Dumbledore was furious.

00:00:55.181 --> 00:00:57.879
As soon as he saved you,
he sent them straight off.

00:00:57.922 --> 00:00:59.533
RON:
There's, uh,
something else

00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:01.230
you should know, too, Harry.

00:01:01.274 --> 00:01:03.624
Um, when you fell, your broom,

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:08.063
it-it sort of blew into
the Whomping Willow and...

00:01:08.107 --> 00:01:10.283
well, it's, uh...

00:01:10.326 --> 00:01:12.894
LUPIN [ voice-over]:
I'm sorry to hear

00:01:12.937 --> 00:01:14.113
about your broomstick.

00:01:14.156 --> 00:01:16.332
Is there no chance
of fixing it?

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.899
No.

00:01:17.942 --> 00:01:21.381
Professor, why do the
dementors affect me so?

00:01:21.424 --> 00:01:23.644
I mean, more than
everyone else?

00:01:23.687 --> 00:01:26.647
Listen, the dementors
are amongst the foulest

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.388
creatures to walk this earth.

00:01:28.431 --> 00:01:32.479
They feed on every good feeling,
every happy memory,

00:01:32.522 --> 00:01:36.265
until a person is left
with absolutely nothing

00:01:36.309 --> 00:01:38.572
but his worst experiences.

00:01:38.615 --> 00:01:41.618
You are not weak, Harry.

00:01:41.662 --> 00:01:44.578
The dementors
affect you most of all

00:01:44.621 --> 00:01:46.971
because there are
true horrors in your past.

00:01:47.015 --> 00:01:49.887
Horrors your classmates
can scarcely imagine.

00:01:49.931 --> 00:01:52.716
You have nothing
to be ashamed of.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.196
I'm scared,
Professor.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.546
Well, I'd consider you
a fool if you weren't.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.940
I need to know how
to fight them.

00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:00.594
You could
teach me.

00:02:00.637 --> 00:02:03.249
You made that dementor
on the train go away.

00:02:03.292 --> 00:02:04.815
There was only one that night.

00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:06.252
But you made it
go away.

00:02:06.295 --> 00:02:09.733
Well, I don't pretend
to be an expert, Harry,

00:02:09.777 --> 00:02:12.432
but as the dementors
seem to have developed

00:02:12.475 --> 00:02:14.521
a particular
interest in you,

00:02:14.564 --> 00:02:16.958
perhaps
I should teach you.

00:02:17.001 --> 00:02:19.047
But after
the holidays.

00:02:19.091 --> 00:02:21.963
For now,
I need to rest.

00:02:31.538 --> 00:02:35.890
♪

00:02:40.503 --> 00:02:43.550
[ bell tolling]

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.295
Last call for Hogsmeade!
Come on, now!

00:02:49.338 --> 00:02:52.559
Hogwarts or Hogsmeade!
Make your bloody minds up!

00:02:52.602 --> 00:02:56.345
[ indistinct shouting]

00:02:56.389 --> 00:02:58.652
[ footsteps]

00:02:58.695 --> 00:03:03.047
[ distant conversation]

00:03:06.268 --> 00:03:07.661
HARRY:
Guys, let me go!

00:03:07.704 --> 00:03:08.705
Oh, clever, Harry.

00:03:08.749 --> 00:03:09.793
But not clever
enough.

00:03:09.837 --> 00:03:11.752
Besides, we've got
a better way.

00:03:11.795 --> 00:03:12.970
HARRY:
Guys, come on!

00:03:13.014 --> 00:03:14.015
I'm trying
to get to Hogsmeade!

00:03:14.058 --> 00:03:15.234
BOTH:
We know.

00:03:15.277 --> 00:03:16.235
Don't worry.We'll get you there.

00:03:16.278 --> 00:03:17.410
We'll show you
a quicker way.

00:03:17.453 --> 00:03:18.411
If you pipe down.

00:03:18.454 --> 00:03:20.108
Ow!Aw, bless him.

00:03:20.152 --> 00:03:21.196
HARRY:
Let me go!

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.198
Come on, guys. Don't...

00:03:23.242 --> 00:03:24.504
Now, Harry.

00:03:24.547 --> 00:03:26.070
BOTH:
Come and join the big boys.

00:03:26.114 --> 00:03:27.289
[ grunting]

00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:28.595
What are you doing?

00:03:28.638 --> 00:03:29.683
Shh!

00:03:29.726 --> 00:03:31.293
What's this rubbish?

00:03:31.337 --> 00:03:32.555
[ chuckles]:
What's this rubbish, he says.

00:03:32.599 --> 00:03:34.253
That there is the secret
to our success.

00:03:34.296 --> 00:03:36.080
It's a wrench giving
it to you, believe me.

00:03:36.124 --> 00:03:38.866
But, we've decided, your
needs are greater than ours.

00:03:38.909 --> 00:03:40.476
George, if you will.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:45.307
I solemnly swear that
I am up to no good.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.790
"Messieurs Mooney,
Wormtail,

00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:53.228
"Padfoot and Prongs
are proud to present

00:03:53.272 --> 00:03:55.230
The Marauder's Map."

00:03:55.274 --> 00:03:57.406
We owe them so much.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:04.065
Hang on.
This is Hogwarts.

00:04:04.108 --> 00:04:06.023
And that...
No.

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:07.286
Is that really...

00:04:07.329 --> 00:04:09.070
Dumbledore. Pacing.In his study.

00:04:09.113 --> 00:04:10.289
Does that
a lot.

00:04:10.332 --> 00:04:12.247
HARRY:
So you mean,
this map shows...

00:04:12.291 --> 00:04:13.857
Everyone.Everyone?

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:15.119
Everyone.Where they are.

00:04:15.163 --> 00:04:16.120
What they're doing.

00:04:16.164 --> 00:04:17.296
Every minute.Of every day.

00:04:17.339 --> 00:04:18.732
Brilliant!
Where'd you get it?

00:04:18.775 --> 00:04:19.820
Nicked it from Filch's
office, of course.

00:04:19.863 --> 00:04:20.908
First year.

00:04:20.951 --> 00:04:22.214
Now, listen.

00:04:22.257 --> 00:04:22.997
There are seven
secret passageways

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:23.867
out of the castle.

00:04:23.911 --> 00:04:24.781
We'd recommend...

00:04:24.825 --> 00:04:26.000
BOTH:
This one.

00:04:26.043 --> 00:04:27.523
The One-Eyed
Witch passageway.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.090
It'll lead you straight
to Honeyduke's Cellar.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:30.787
But you best hurry.
Filch is heading this way.

00:04:30.831 --> 00:04:32.267
Oh, and Harry,
don't forget.

00:04:32.311 --> 00:04:34.356
When you're done, just
give it a tap and say...

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.402
BOTH:
Mischief managed.

00:04:36.445 --> 00:04:39.143
Otherwise, anyone can read it.

00:04:45.976 --> 00:04:47.978
[ clattering]

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.071
[ stairs creaking]

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.780
♪

00:05:06.823 --> 00:05:09.478
[ stairs creaking]

00:05:09.522 --> 00:05:11.393
[ register ringing]

00:05:11.437 --> 00:05:16.529
[ indistinct conversations]

00:05:23.927 --> 00:05:25.146
Delicious.

00:05:25.189 --> 00:05:27.061
I know.[ bell ringing]

00:05:32.806 --> 00:05:36.331
HERMIONE:
It's meant to be the most
haunted building in Britain.

00:05:36.375 --> 00:05:37.811
Did I mention that?

00:05:37.854 --> 00:05:38.986
[ chuckles]

00:05:39.029 --> 00:05:40.161
RON:
Twice.

00:05:40.204 --> 00:05:41.293
Oh.

00:05:41.336 --> 00:05:42.424
Do you want to move
a bit closer?

00:05:42.468 --> 00:05:43.338
Huh?

00:05:43.382 --> 00:05:44.687
To the Shrieking
Shack.

00:05:44.731 --> 00:05:47.516
Oh-Oh, actually,
I'm... I'm fine here.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.996
DRACO:
Well, well,

00:05:49.039 --> 00:05:50.258
look who's here.

00:05:50.302 --> 00:05:52.260
You two shopping for
your new dream home?

00:05:52.304 --> 00:05:54.262
Bit grand for you,
isn't it Weasle-Bee?

00:05:54.306 --> 00:05:57.265
Don't your family
sleep in, uh, one room?

00:05:57.309 --> 00:05:59.093
Shut your mouth, Malfoy.

00:05:59.136 --> 00:06:00.573
Ooh, not very friendly.

00:06:00.616 --> 00:06:02.792
Boys, I think it's time
we teach Weasle-Bee

00:06:02.836 --> 00:06:04.751
how to respect his superiors.

00:06:04.794 --> 00:06:05.969
[ Hermione chuckles]

00:06:06.013 --> 00:06:07.493
Hope you don't mean yourself.

00:06:07.536 --> 00:06:09.364
How dare you talk to me?

00:06:09.408 --> 00:06:12.541
You filthy little mudblood.

00:06:15.936 --> 00:06:17.503
Who's there?!

00:06:20.157 --> 00:06:22.334
[ grunting]

00:06:22.769 --> 00:06:23.639
Don't just
stand there,

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:25.467
do something.What?!

00:06:25.511 --> 00:06:27.730
[ gasping]

00:06:29.906 --> 00:06:30.690
[ yells]

00:06:30.733 --> 00:06:32.039
[ chuckles]

00:06:32.387 --> 00:06:34.215
[ gasps]

00:06:34.258 --> 00:06:36.304
[ yells]

00:06:36.348 --> 00:06:38.219
[ yelling]

00:06:41.527 --> 00:06:43.398
[ yelling]

00:06:45.574 --> 00:06:47.315
RON:
What's up, Malfoy?
Lost your skis?

00:06:47.359 --> 00:06:51.363
[ panting]

00:06:51.885 --> 00:06:53.974
Get out of the way!

00:06:54.017 --> 00:06:55.062
Move!

00:06:55.105 --> 00:06:58.979
CRABBE:
Malfoy! Wait! Wait!

00:06:59.022 --> 00:07:01.938
[ laughing]

00:07:01.982 --> 00:07:03.505
Harry!

00:07:03.549 --> 00:07:04.724
[ laughing]

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:05.812
Bloody hell, Harry.

00:07:05.855 --> 00:07:08.205
That was not funny.

00:07:08.249 --> 00:07:09.424
[ laughing]

00:07:09.468 --> 00:07:10.817
RON:
Those weasels.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.906
Never told me about
any Marauder's Map.

00:07:12.949 --> 00:07:14.124
HERMIONE:
But Harry isn't

00:07:14.168 --> 00:07:15.648
going to keep it.

00:07:15.691 --> 00:07:17.432
He's going to turn it over
to Professor McGonagall.

00:07:17.476 --> 00:07:18.302
Aren't you?

00:07:18.346 --> 00:07:19.478
RON:
Oh, sure.

00:07:19.521 --> 00:07:20.827
Along with
his Invisibility Cloak.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.917
Oh, look who it is.
Madam Rosmerta.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.266
Ron
fancies her.

00:07:25.309 --> 00:07:26.441
RON:
That's not true.

00:07:26.485 --> 00:07:27.921
Professor McGonagall!Cornelius!

00:07:27.964 --> 00:07:29.139
HAGRID:
Allow me, Minister.

00:07:29.183 --> 00:07:31.620
Oh, Hagrid.Sorry about that.

00:07:31.664 --> 00:07:32.969
Rosmerta, my dear.

00:07:33.013 --> 00:07:34.449
I hope
business is good.

00:07:34.493 --> 00:07:37.147
It'd be a lot better
if the Ministry wasn't

00:07:37.191 --> 00:07:41.151
sending dementors into
my pub every other night!

00:07:41.195 --> 00:07:42.849
We... have...

00:07:42.892 --> 00:07:45.112
We have a killer
on the loose.

00:07:45.155 --> 00:07:46.940
Oh, Sirius Black
in Hogsmeade!

00:07:46.983 --> 00:07:49.377
And what would
bring him here?

00:07:49.421 --> 00:07:51.335
[ whispering]:
Harry Potter.

00:07:51.379 --> 00:07:53.076
Harry Potter?!

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.687
Shh!

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:55.470
Come.

00:07:55.514 --> 00:07:58.342
[ gasps]

00:07:58.386 --> 00:07:59.953
Harry!

00:07:59.996 --> 00:08:01.345
Oh, I say.

